@startuml uc03-misuse-case
' Use Case 3 (Misuse) -- Search Destination and Select Dates
' CHANGED FOR THE RECOMMENDATION FEATURE:
'   - Added the two mitigations we actually implemented, so this slide matches
'     the "mitigates" pattern used on the other misuse-case slides:
'       * Internal Token Authentication  -> the browser can never reach FastAPI
'       * Validate & Allowlist Events    -> fake telemetry cannot poison ranking
'   - Added "Fabricated Recommendation Claims" as a misuse, mitigated by
'     deterministic, retrieval-grounded explanations (no LLM at request time).
' Everything else is unchanged.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam usecaseBackgroundColor #EEEEEE
skinparam usecaseBorderColor Black
skinparam actorBackgroundColor White
skinparam actorBorderColor Black
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica

actor Attacker <<misuser>> #red
actor User
actor "Hotel Search API" as HotelAPI
actor "Recommendation Engine" as RecEngine

rectangle "Ascenda Hotel Booking Platform" {
  usecase "UC-03: Search Destination & Select Dates" as UC03
  usecase "Suggest Ranked Destinations" as Suggest
  usecase "Select Dates, Guests & Rooms" as SelectDates

  usecase "<<misuse>>\nAPI Scraping / Automated Traffic" as Scraping #FFCCCC
  usecase "<<misuse>>\nRecommendation Engine Manipulation" as Manipulation #FFCCCC
  usecase "<<misuse>>\nFabricated Recommendation Claims" as Fabrication #FFCCCC

  usecase "Internal Token Authentication" as TokenAuth
  usecase "Validate & Allowlist Events" as EventAllowlist
  usecase "Deterministic Grounded Explanations" as Grounded
}

User --> UC03
Attacker --> Scraping
Attacker --> Manipulation
Attacker --> Fabrication

Scraping ..> UC03 : threatens
Manipulation ..> Suggest : threatens
Fabrication ..> Suggest : threatens

UC03 ..> Suggest : include
UC03 ..> SelectDates : include

Suggest --> HotelAPI
Suggest --> RecEngine

' NEW: mitigations actually implemented
TokenAuth ..> Manipulation : mitigates
EventAllowlist ..> Manipulation : mitigates
Grounded ..> Fabrication : mitigates

@enduml
